{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> This is a wonder, for figs are harmful to a boil, and this is what the prophet said. Some say that they are by commandment." "<b>A cake of figs.</b> Pressed cakes, and they shall be cut with a knife." "<b>And they shall spread it.</b> Close in the language of Kedar, and its meaning is known."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:57.580445377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}